    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0265" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4470: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor
                        n="49" xml:id="d198-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-20T16:00:00+01:00">May 20, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 20—11:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>173. Department’s 46, May 19, 6 p.m.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d198-f2"/> Italian
                    papers today publish reports from Addis Ababa to the effect that according to
                    accounts <pb facs="0266" n="201" xml:id="pg201"/> from Italian airmen who are
                    said to be maintaining surveillance throughout the entire country and from
                    caravans reaching Addis Ababa during the past few days from Gimma, Caffa and
                    Gambella the rumors as to an Ethiopian troop movement toward Addis Ababa on the
                    western borders with the support of Sudanese contingents under the command of an
                    Ethiopian Prince are false. Reports add that the attitude of Ras Imru who, in
                    command of a few hundred warriors, had taken refuge near the Godjam border is
                    becoming less hostile. One editorial mentions Ras Imru as probably the only
                    chieftain alive who has not fled the country or submitted to Italy and that his
                    fate will soon be decided.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d198-f1" n="49" type="source" xml:id="d198-f1-content">
